<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><Content><Views><ViewDef id="38957c6d-0f1d-432e-85fb-683272cf3383"><Title>[VCF Content Factory] VM Snapshot Inventory</Title><Description>Per-snapshot inventory for VMWARE Virtual Machines: one row per snapshot instance (GROUP_diskspace fan-out), with Snapshot Name, Age (Days), Snapshot Space (GB), Creator, Description, plus flat Parent Cluster, Parent vCenter, Parent Datastore, and Total Snapshot Space (GB).
One row per LIVE snapshot older than 24h, the instanced-key subject filter below drops ghost/deleted-snapshot rows per-row. Instanced properties populate ~24h after snapshot creation; Age -1 = deleted or &lt;24h old, so snapshots younger than 24h don't appear, a recall gap, not a bug. Sort descending on Age (or Total Snapshot Space (GB) as a proxy) at the consuming widget (sort_by_column/sort_by_dir); no view-level default.
